  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Samuel",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 13,
    "summary": "Saul offers a burnt offering—The Lord rejects him and chooses another captain over His people.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Saul reigned one year; and when he had reigned two years over Israel,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 13:1",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Saul chose him three thousand men of Israel; whereof two thousand were with Saul in Michmash and in mount Beth-el, and a thousand were with Jonathan in Gibeah of Benjamin: and the rest of the people he sent every man to his tent.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 13:2",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jonathan smote the garrison of the Philistines that was in Geba, and the Philistines heard of it. And Saul blew the trumpet throughout all the land, saying, Let the Hebrews hear.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 101
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 13:3",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And all Israel heard say that Saul had smitten a garrison of the Philistines, and that Israel also was had in abomination with the Philistines. And the people were called together after Saul to Gilgal.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 13:4",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Philistines gathered themselves together to fight with Israel, thirty thousand chariots, and six thousand horsemen, and people as the sand which is on the sea shore in multitude: and they came up, and pitched in Michmash, eastward from Beth-aven.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 153,
            "end": 155
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 13:5",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "When the men of Israel saw that they were in a strait, (for the people were distressed,) then the people did hide themselves in caves, and in thickets, and in rocks, and in high places, and in pits.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 113,
            "text": "1 Sam. 14:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 133,
            "text": "1 Sam. 14:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
